<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwYw"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Outside_Lever_House,_Port_Sunlight_(2).jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwZA"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Outside_Lever_House,_Port_Sunlight_(2).jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Outside_Lever_House%2C_Port_Sunlight_%282%29.jpg/250px-Outside_Lever_House%2C_Port_Sunlight_%282%29.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="800" data-file-height="600" data-file-type="bitmap" height="188" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Outside_Lever_House%2C_Port_Sunlight_%282%29.jpg/500px-Outside_Lever_House%2C_Port_Sunlight_%282%29.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwZQ"/></a><figcaption id="mwZg">Lever House in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Sunlight" title="Port Sunlight" id="mwZw">Port Sunlight</a>, United Kingdom, the former headquarters of Lever Brothers</figcaption></figure>

<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwaA" aria-labelledby="1930–1940"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="1930–1940"><span id="1930.E2.80.931940" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>1930–1940</h3></div>
<p id="mwaQ">Unilever was formed by a merger of Dutch <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margarine_Unie" title="Margarine Unie" id="mwag">Margarine Unie</a> and British soapmaker <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lever_Brothers" title="Lever Brothers" id="mwaw">Lever Brothers</a> in 1930, with the name of Unilever a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blend_word" title="Blend word" class="mw-redirect" id="mwbA">blend word</a> of the name of both companies.<sup about="#mwt54" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-10" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-10" id="mwbQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwbg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbw">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwcQ">In the 1930s, the business grew, and new ventures were launched in Africa and Latin America. During this time, Unilever acquired the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Africa_Company" title="United Africa Company" id="mwcg">United Africa Company</a>, created from a merger of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/African_&amp;_Eastern_Trade_Corporation" title="African &amp; Eastern Trade Corporation" id="mwcw">African &amp; Eastern Trade Corporation</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Royal_Niger_Company" title="Royal Niger Company" id="mwdA">Royal Niger Company</a>, which oversaw British trade interests in present-day Nigeria during the colonial era.<sup about="#mwt57" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-11" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-11" id="mwdQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdw">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mweA">]</span></span></a></sup>
The Nazi occupation of Europe during the Second World War meant that Unilever was unable to reinvest its capital into Europe, so it instead acquired new businesses in the United Kingdom and the United States.<sup about="#mwt60" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Wubs154_12-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Wubs154"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Wubs154-12"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Wubs154-12" id="mweQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mweg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwew">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwfQ">In 1943, it acquired <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Lipton" title="Thomas Lipton" id="mwfg">T. J. Lipton</a>, a majority stake in Frosted Foods (owner of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birds_Eye" title="Birds Eye" id="mwfw">Birds Eye</a> brand in the United Kingdom)<sup about="#mwt63" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-13"}}'><a href="#cite_note-13" id="mwgA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwgQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgg">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgw">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batchelors_Peas" title="Batchelors Peas" class="mw-redirect" id="mwhA">Batchelors Peas</a>, one of the largest vegetables canners in the United Kingdom.<sup about="#mwt66" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated3_14-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated3"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-autogenerated3-14"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated3-14" id="mwhQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwhg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwhw">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt69" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-hbs.edu_15-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"hbs.edu"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-hbs.edu-15"}}'><a href="#cite_note-hbs.edu-15" id="mwiQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwig"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiw">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjA">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1944, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pepsodent" title="Pepsodent" id="mwjQ">Pepsodent</a> was acquired.<sup about="#mwt70" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-hbs.edu_15-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"hbs.edu"}}'><a href="#cite_note-hbs.edu-15" id="mwjg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwjw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkA">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwkg">In 1933, Unilever Indonesia was established in December as Lever Zeepfabrieken N.V. and had operations in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cikarang" title="Cikarang" id="mwkw">Cikarang</a>, West Java at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rungkut" title="Rungkut" id="mwlA">Rungkut</a>, East Java and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Sumatra" title="North Sumatra" id="mwlQ">North Sumatra</a>.<sup about="#mwt73" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-16"}}'><a href="#cite_note-16" id="mwlg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwlw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwmA">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwmQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwmg" aria-labelledby="1941–1960"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="1941–1960"><span id="1941.E2.80.931960" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>1941–1960</h3></div>
<p id="mwmw">After 1945, Unilever's American businesses (Lever Brothers and T.J. Lipton) began to decline.<sup about="#mwt77" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated1_17-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-autogenerated1-17"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated1-17" id="mwnA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwnQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwng">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnw">]</span></span></a></sup> As a result, Unilever began to operate a "hands-off" policy towards the subsidiaries and left American management to its own devices.<sup about="#mwt78" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated1_17-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated1-17" id="mwoA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwoQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwog">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwow">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwpA">Sunsilk was first launched in the United Kingdom in 1954.<sup about="#mwt81" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ThainBradley426_18-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ThainBradley426"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ThainBradley426-18"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ThainBradley426-18" id="mwpQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwpg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwpw">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqA">]</span></span></a></sup> Dove was first launched in the US in 1957.<sup about="#mwt82" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-ThainBradley426_18-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"ThainBradley426"}}'><a href="#cite_note-ThainBradley426-18" id="mwqQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwqg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqw">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrA">]</span></span></a></sup> Unilever took full ownership of Frosted Foods in 1957, which it renamed <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Birds_Eye" title="Birds Eye" id="mwrQ">Birds Eye</a>.<sup about="#mwt85" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HensmansJohnson139_19-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HensmansJohnson139"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HensmansJohnson139-19"}}'><a href="#cite_note-HensmansJohnson139-19" id="mwrg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwrw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsA">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The US-based <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Good_Humor" title="Good Humor" id="mwsg">Good Humor</a> ice cream business was acquired in 1961.<sup about="#mwt88" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-20" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-20"}}'><a href="#cite_note-20" id="mwsw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtQ">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtg">]</span></span></a></sup> By the mid-1960s, laundry soap and edible fats still contributed around half of Unilever's corporate profits.<sup about="#mwt89" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated3_14-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated3-14" id="mwtw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwuA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuQ">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwug">]</span></span></a></sup> However, a stagnant market for yellow fats (butter, margarine, and similar products) and increasing competition in detergents and soaps from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Procter_&amp;_Gamble" title="Procter &amp; Gamble" id="mwuw">Procter &amp; Gamble</a> forced Unilever to diversify.<sup about="#mwt90" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated3_14-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated3-14" id="mwvA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvg">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvw">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1971, Unilever acquired the British-based <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lipton" title="Lipton" id="mwwA">Lipton Ltd</a> from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Home_and_Colonial_Stores" title="Home and Colonial Stores" id="mwwQ">Allied Suppliers</a>.<sup about="#mwt91" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated3_14-3" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated3-14" id="mwwg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwww"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxA">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxQ">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1978, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ingredion" title="Ingredion" id="mwxg">National Starch</a> was acquired for $487<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwxw"> </span>million, marking the largest ever foreign-acquisition of a US company at that point.<sup about="#mwt94" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HensmansJohnson140_21-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HensmansJohnson140"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HensmansJohnson140-21"}}'><a href="#cite_note-HensmansJohnson140-21" id="mwyA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwyQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyg">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mwzA" aria-labelledby="1961–1980"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="1961–1980"><span id="1961.E2.80.931980" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>1961–1980</h3></div>
<p id="mwzQ">By the end of the 1970s through acquisitions, Unilever had gained 30 per cent of the Western European ice cream market.<sup about="#mwt95" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated3_14-4" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated3-14" id="mwzg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwzw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0A">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0Q">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1982, Unilever management decided to reposition itself from an unwieldy conglomerate to a more concentrated <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fast-moving_consumer_goods" title="Fast-moving consumer goods" id="mw0g">fast-moving consumer goods</a> (FMCG) company.<sup about="#mwt98" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HensmansJohnson141_22-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HensmansJohnson141"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-HensmansJohnson141-22"}}'><a href="#cite_note-HensmansJohnson141-22" id="mw0w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw1A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1Q">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1g">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw1w">In 1984, Unilever acquired <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brooke_Bond" title="Brooke Bond" id="mw2A">Brooke Bond</a> (maker of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PG_Tips" title="PG Tips" id="mw2Q">PG Tips</a> tea) for £390<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mw2g"> </span>million in the company's first successful <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Takeover" title="Takeover" id="mw2w">takeover</a>.<sup about="#mwt99" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-autogenerated3_14-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"autogenerated3"}}'><a href="#cite_note-autogenerated3-14" id="mw3A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw3Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3g">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3w">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1986, Unilever strengthened its position in the world skin care market by acquiring <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pond's" title="Pond's" id="mw4A">Ponds</a> (merged from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chesebrough_Manufacturing_Company" title="Chesebrough Manufacturing Company" id="mw4Q">Chesebrough Manufacturing</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pond's" title="Pond's" id="mw4g">Pond's Creams</a>), the maker of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ragú" title="Ragú" id="mw4w">Ragú</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pond's" title="Pond's" id="mw5A">Pond's</a>, Aqua-Net, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cutex" title="Cutex" id="mw5Q">Cutex</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vaseline" title="Vaseline" id="mw5g">Vaseline</a> in another hostile takeover.<sup about="#mwt100" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-HensmansJohnson141_22-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"HensmansJohnson141"}}'><a href="#cite_note-HensmansJohnson141-22" id="mw5w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw6A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6Q">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw6g">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1989, Unilever bought Calvin Klein Cosmetics, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fabergé_(cosmetics)" title="Fabergé (cosmetics)" id="mw6w">Fabergé</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elizabeth_Arden,_Inc." title="Elizabeth Arden, Inc." id="mw7A">Elizabeth Arden</a>, but the latter was later sold (in 2000) to FFI Fragrances.<sup about="#mwt103" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nyt1996_23-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nyt1996"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-nyt1996-23"}}'><a href="#cite_note-nyt1996-23" id="mw7Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw7g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7w">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mw8Q" aria-labelledby="1981–2000"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="1981–2000"><span id="1981.E2.80.932000" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>1981–2000</h3></div>
<p id="mw8g">In 1992, Unilever <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghana" title="Ghana" id="mw8w">Ghana</a> was established in July following a merger of UAC Ghana Limited and Lever Brothers Ghana Limited.<sup about="#mwt106" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-GBI_24-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"GBI"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-GBI-24"}}'><a href="#cite_note-GBI-24" id="mw9A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw9Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9g">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9w">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw-A">In 1993, Unilever acquired <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breyers" title="Breyers" id="mw-Q">Breyers</a> from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kraft_Foods_Inc." title="Kraft Foods Inc." id="mw-g">Kraft</a>, which made the company the largest ice cream manufacturer in the United States.<sup about="#mwt109" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Jones2005_25-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Jones2005"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Jones2005-25"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Jones2005-25" id="mw-w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw_A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw_Q">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw_g">]</span></span></a></sup> In the same year, it acquired the Isaly Klondike Company, makers of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Klondike_bar" title="Klondike bar" id="mw_w">Klondike bar</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popsicle_(brand)" title="Popsicle (brand)" id="mwAQA">Popsicle Industries</a>.<sup about="#mwt112" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-26" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-26"}}'><a href="#cite_note-26" id="mwAQE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQM">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAQU">In 1996, Unilever merged Elida Gibbs and Lever Brothers in its UK operations.<sup about="#mwt115" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-27" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-27"}}'><a href="#cite_note-27" id="mwAQY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQg">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQk">]</span></span></a></sup> It also purchased <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Helene_Curtis_Industries,_Inc." title="Helene Curtis Industries, Inc." id="mwAQo">Helene Curtis</a>, significantly expanding its presence in the United States shampoo and deodorant market.<sup about="#mwt116" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nyt1996_23-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nyt1996"}}'><a href="#cite_note-nyt1996-23" id="mwAQs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ0">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ4">]</span></span></a></sup> The purchase brought Unilever the Suave and Finesse hair-care product brands and Degree deodorant brand.<sup about="#mwt117" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-nyt1996_23-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"nyt1996"}}'><a href="#cite_note-nyt1996-23" id="mwAQ8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARE">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwARM">In 1997, Unilever sold its speciality chemicals division, including National Starch &amp; Chemical, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quest_International" title="Quest International" id="mwARQ">Quest</a>, Unichema and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Crosfield" title="Joseph Crosfield" id="mwARU">Crosfield</a> to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial_Chemical_Industries" title="Imperial Chemical Industries" id="mwARY">Imperial Chemical Industries</a> for £4.9<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwARc"> </span>billion.<sup about="#mwt120" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Jones364_28-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Jones364"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Jones364-28"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Jones364-28" id="mwARg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARo">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwARw">In 1998, Unilever established a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sustainable_agriculture" title="Sustainable agriculture" id="mwAR0">sustainable agriculture</a> programme.<sup about="#mwt123" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-29" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-29"}}'><a href="#cite_note-29" id="mwAR4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAR8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASA">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwASI">In 2000, Unilever acquired the boutique mustard retailer Maille,<sup about="#mwt126" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-30" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-30"}}'><a href="#cite_note-30" id="mwASM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASU">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASY">]</span></span></a></sup> Ben &amp; Jerry's and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SlimFast" title="SlimFast" id="mwASc">SlimFast</a> for £1.63<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwASg"> </span>billion,<sup about="#mwt129" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-31" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-31"}}'><a href="#cite_note-31" id="mwASk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASs">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt132" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-32" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-32"}}'><a href="#cite_note-32" id="mwAS0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAS4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAS8">[</span>32<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATA">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hellmann's_and_Best_Foods" title="Hellmann's and Best Foods" id="mwATE">Bestfoods</a> for £13.4<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwATI"> </span>billion.<sup about="#mwt135" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_33-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:1-33"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-33" id="mwATM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATU">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATY">]</span></span></a></sup> The Bestfoods acquisition increased Unilever's scale in foods in America, and added brands including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knorr_(brand)" title="Knorr (brand)" id="mwATc">Knorr</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marmite" title="Marmite" id="mwATg">Marmite</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bovril" title="Bovril" id="mwATk">Bovril</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hellmann's_and_Best_Foods" title="Hellmann's and Best Foods" id="mwATo">Hellmann's</a> to its portfolio.<sup about="#mwt136" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_33-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-33" id="mwATs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAT0">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAT4">]</span></span></a></sup> In exchange for European regulatory approval of the deal, Unilever divested itself of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxo_(food)" title="Oxo (food)" id="mwAT8">Oxo</a>, Lesieur, McDonnells, Bla Band, Royco, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Batchelors" title="Batchelors" id="mwAUA">Batchelors</a>.<sup about="#mwt139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-34" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-34"}}'><a href="#cite_note-34" id="mwAUE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUM">[</span>34<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt142" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-35" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-35"}}'><a href="#cite_note-35" id="mwAUU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUc">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwAUk" aria-labelledby="2001–2010"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="2001–2010"><span id="2001.E2.80.932010" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>2001–2010</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAUo"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Unilever-jobs-00-08.svg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAUs"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Unilever-jobs-00-08.svg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Unilever-jobs-00-08.svg/250px-Unilever-jobs-00-08.svg.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="400" data-file-height="400" data-file-type="drawing" height="250" width="250" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Unilever-jobs-00-08.svg/500px-Unilever-jobs-00-08.svg.png 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAUw"/></a><figcaption id="mwAU0"><b id="mwAU4">Global employment at Unilever 2000–08</b><br id="mwAU8"/> Black represents employment numbers in Europe, light grey represents the Americas and dark grey represents Asia and Africa.<br id="mwAVA"/>Between 2000 and 2008 Unilever reduced global workforce numbers by 41%, from 295,000 to 174,000.<br id="mwAVE"/>
Notes: Europe figures for 2000–2003 are all Europe; from 2004 figures in black are Western Europe. For 2004–2008 figures for Asia and Africa include Eastern and Central Europe.<br id="mwAVI"/><i id="mwAVM">Source: Unilever Annual Reports 2004, 2008</i></figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwAVQ">In 2001, Unilever split into two divisions: one for foods and one for home and personal care.<sup about="#mwt145" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-36" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-36"}}'><a href="#cite_note-36" id="mwAVU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVc">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVg">]</span></span></a></sup> In the United Kingdom, it merged its Lever Brothers and Elida Fabergé businesses as Lever Fabergé in January 2001.<sup about="#mwt148" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-37" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-37"}}'><a href="#cite_note-37" id="mwAVk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVs">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAV0">In 2003, Unilever announced the sale of the Dalda brand in both India and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pakistan" title="Pakistan" id="mwAV4">Pakistan</a>.<sup about="#mwt151" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:02_38-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":02"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:02-38"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:02-38" id="mwAV8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWE">[</span>38<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWI">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2003, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bunge_Global" title="Bunge Global" id="mwAWM">Bunge Limited</a> acquired the Dalda brand from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hindustan_Unilever" title="Hindustan Unilever" id="mwAWQ">Hindustan Unilever Limited</a> for reportedly under Rs. 1<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAWU"> </span>billion.<sup about="#mwt154" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BS_39-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BS"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BS-39"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BS-39" id="mwAWY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWg">[</span>39<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWk">]</span></span></a></sup> On 30 March 2004, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unilever_Pakistan" title="Unilever Pakistan" id="mwAWo">Unilever Pakistan</a> accepted an offer of Rs. 1.33<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAWs"> </span>billion for the sale of its Dalda brand and related business of edible oils and fats to the newly incorporated company Dalda Foods (Pvt.) Limited.<sup about="#mwt157" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Dawn_40-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Dawn"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Dawn-40"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Dawn-40" id="mwAWw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAW0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW4">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAXA">In 2002, the company sold its speciality oils and fats division, known as Loders Croklaan, for RM814<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAXE"> </span>million (€218.5<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAXI"> </span>million) to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IOI_Group" title="IOI Group" id="mwAXM">IOI Corporation</a>, a Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia–based oil palm company. As part of the deal, the Loders Croklaan name was maintained.<sup about="#mwt160" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-41" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-41"}}'><a href="#cite_note-41" id="mwAXQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXY">[</span>41<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXc">]</span></span></a></sup> Unilever sold the brands Mazola, Argo &amp; Kingsfords, Karo, Golden Griddle, and Henri's, along with several of its Canadian brands, to ACH Food Companies, an American subsidiary of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Associated_British_Foods" title="Associated British Foods" id="mwAXg">Associated British Foods</a>.<sup about="#mwt163" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-42" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-42"}}'><a href="#cite_note-42" id="mwAXk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXs">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAX0">In 2004, Unilever Bangladesh, established in 1964,<sup about="#mwt166" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-43" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-43"}}'><a href="#cite_note-43" id="mwAX4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAX8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYA">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYE">]</span></span></a></sup> changed its former name Lever Brothers Bangladesh Ltd to its present name in December.<sup about="#mwt169" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-44" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-44"}}'><a href="#cite_note-44" id="mwAYI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYQ">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYU">]</span></span></a></sup> It is owned 60.4% by Unilever and 39.6% by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_Bangladesh" title="Government of Bangladesh" id="mwAYY">Government of Bangladesh</a>.<sup about="#mwt172" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-45" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-45"}}'><a href="#cite_note-45" id="mwAYc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYk">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt175" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-46" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-46"}}'><a href="#cite_note-46" id="mwAYs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAY0">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAY4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAY8">In 2007, Unilever partnered with <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rainforest_Alliance" title="Rainforest Alliance" id="mwAZA">Rainforest Alliance</a> to sustainably source all its tea.<sup about="#mwt178" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-47" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-47"}}'><a href="#cite_note-47" id="mwAZE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZM">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAZU">In 2009, Unilever agreed to acquire the personal care business of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sara_Lee_Corporation" title="Sara Lee Corporation" id="mwAZY">Sara Lee Corporation</a>, including brands such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radox" title="Radox" id="mwAZc">Radox</a>, Badedas and Duschdas.<sup about="#mwt181" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-48" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-48"}}'><a href="#cite_note-48" id="mwAZg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZo">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZs">]</span></span></a></sup> The Sara Lee acquisition was completed on 6 December 2010.<sup about="#mwt184" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-49" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-49"}}'><a href="#cite_note-49" id="mwAZw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZ0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ4">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAaA">In 2010, Unilever acquired the Diplom-Is in Denmark,<sup about="#mwt187" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-50" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-50"}}'><a href="#cite_note-50" id="mwAaE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAaI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaM">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Unilever announced that it had entered into a definitive agreement to sell its consumer tomato products business in Brazil to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cargill" title="Cargill" id="mwAaU">Cargill</a>,<sup about="#mwt190" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-51"}}'><a href="#cite_note-51" id="mwAaY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAac"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAag">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAak">]</span></span></a></sup> purchased <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alberto-Culver" title="Alberto-Culver" id="mwAao">Alberto-Culver</a>, a maker of personal care and household products including Simple, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alberto-Culver" title="Alberto-Culver" id="mwAas">VO5</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alberto-Culver" title="Alberto-Culver" id="mwAaw">Nexxus</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TRESemmé" title="TRESemmé" id="mwAa0">TRESemmé</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mrs._Dash" title="Mrs. Dash" id="mwAa4">Mrs. Dash</a>, for US$3.7<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAa8"> </span>billion.<sup about="#mwt193" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-52" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-52"}}'><a href="#cite_note-52" id="mwAbA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbI">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbM">]</span></span></a></sup> acquired <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evga_S.A" title="Evga S.A" id="mwAbQ">EVGA</a>'s ice cream brands, which included Scandal, Variete and Karabola, and its distribution network in Greece, for an undisclosed amount.<sup about="#mwt196" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-53" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-53"}}'><a href="#cite_note-53" id="mwAbU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbc">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwAbk" aria-labelledby="2011–2020"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="2011–2020"><span id="2011.E2.80.932020" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>2011–2020</h3></div>
<p id="mwAbo">In 2012, Unilever announced it would phase out the use of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microplastics" title="Microplastics" id="mwAbs">microplastics</a> in the form of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microbeads" title="Microbeads" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAbw">microbeads</a> in their personal care products by 2015.<sup about="#mwt199" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-54" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-54"}}'><a href="#cite_note-54" id="mwAb0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAb4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAb8">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAcE">In 2014, Unilever agreed to acquire a majority stake in the China-based water purification company Qinyuan for an undisclosed price,<sup about="#mwt202" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-55" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-55"}}'><a href="#cite_note-55" id="mwAcI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcQ">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcU">]</span></span></a></sup> acquired Talenti Gelato &amp; Sorbetto,<sup about="#mwt205" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-56" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-56"}}'><a href="#cite_note-56" id="mwAcY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcg">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAck">]</span></span></a></sup> acquired <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camay" title="Camay" id="mwAco">Camay</a> brand globally and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zest_(brand)" title="Zest (brand)" id="mwAcs">Zest</a> brand outside of North America and the Caribbean from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Procter_&amp;_Gamble" title="Procter &amp; Gamble" id="mwAcw">Procter &amp; Gamble</a>.<sup about="#mwt208" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-57" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-57"}}'><a href="#cite_note-57" id="mwAc0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAc4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAc8">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAdE">In 2015, Unilever acquired British niche skincare brand REN Skincare,<sup about="#mwt211" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-58" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-58"}}'><a href="#cite_note-58" id="mwAdI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdQ">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdU">]</span></span></a></sup> This was followed in May 2015 by the acquisition of Kate Somerville Skincare.<sup about="#mwt214" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-59" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-59"}}'><a href="#cite_note-59" id="mwAdY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdg">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdk">]</span></span></a></sup> The company also acquired the Italian premium ice cream maker <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grom_(company)" title="Grom (company)" id="mwAdo">GROM</a> for an undisclosed amount.<sup about="#mwt217" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-60" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-60"}}'><a href="#cite_note-60" id="mwAds"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd0">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd4">]</span></span></a></sup> Unilever also separated its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spread_(food)" title="Spread (food)" id="mwAd8">food spreads</a> business,<sup about="#mwt220" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-61" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-61"}}'><a href="#cite_note-61" id="mwAeA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeI">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeM">]</span></span></a></sup> including its <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flora_(spread)" title="Flora (spread)" id="mwAeQ">Flora</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Can't_Believe_It's_Not_Butter!" title="I Can't Believe It's Not Butter!" id="mwAeU">I Can't Believe It's Not Butter!</a> brands, into a standalone entity named Unilever Baking, Cooking and Spreading.<sup about="#mwt223" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-62" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-62"}}'><a href="#cite_note-62" id="mwAeY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAec"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeg">[</span>62<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAek">]</span></span></a></sup> The separation was first announced in December 2014 and was made in response to declining worldwide sales in that product category.<sup about="#mwt224" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-boyle2014_8-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"boyle2014"}}'><a href="#cite_note-boyle2014-8" id="mwAeo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAes"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAew">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAe0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAe4">Unilever bought the United States–based <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Startup_company" title="Startup company" id="mwAe8">startup</a> company <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dollar_Shave_Club" title="Dollar Shave Club" id="mwAfA">Dollar Shave Club</a> for a reported $1<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAfE"> </span>billion (£764<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAfI"> </span>million) to compete in the male grooming market.<sup about="#mwt227" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-63" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-63"}}'><a href="#cite_note-63" id="mwAfM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfU">[</span>63<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfY">]</span></span></a></sup> On 16 August 2016, Unilever acquired Blueair, a Swedish supplier of mobile indoor air purification technologies.<sup about="#mwt230" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-64" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-64"}}'><a href="#cite_note-64" id="mwAfc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfk">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfo">]</span></span></a></sup> In July 2024, Blueair received a warning letter from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Trade_Commission" title="Federal Trade Commission" id="mwAfs">Federal Trade Commission</a> concerning warranty restrictions related to use of certain replacement filters.<sup about="#mwt233" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-65" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-65"}}'><a href="#cite_note-65" id="mwAfw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAf0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAf4">[</span>65<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAf8">]</span></span></a></sup> In September 2016, Unilever acquired <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seventh_Generation_Inc." title="Seventh Generation Inc." id="mwAgA">Seventh Generation Inc.</a> for $700<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAgE"> </span>million.<sup about="#mwt236" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Wall_Street_Journal:_Unilever_Buys_‘Green’_Products_Maker_Seventh_Generation_66-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Wall Street Journal: Unilever Buys ‘Green’ Products Maker Seventh Generation"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Wall_Street_Journal:_Unilever_Buys_‘Green’_Products_Maker_Seventh_Generation-66"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Wall_Street_Journal:_Unilever_Buys_‘Green’_Products_Maker_Seventh_Generation-66" id="mwAgI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgQ">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgU">]</span></span></a></sup> On 16 December 2016, Unilever acquired Living Proof Inc, a hair care products business.<sup about="#mwt239" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-67" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-67"}}'><a href="#cite_note-67" id="mwAgY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgg">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAgo">In 2017, significantly smaller <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kraft_Heinz" title="Kraft Heinz" id="mwAgs">Kraft Heinz</a> made a $143-billion bid for Unilever.<sup about="#mwt242" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-68" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-68"}}'><a href="#cite_note-68" id="mwAgw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAg0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAg4">[</span>68<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAg8">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt245" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-69" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-69"}}'><a href="#cite_note-69" id="mwAhA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhI">[</span>69<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhM">]</span></span></a></sup> The deal was declined by Unilever.<sup about="#mwt248" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-70" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-70"}}'><a href="#cite_note-70" id="mwAhQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhY">[</span>70<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhc">]</span></span></a></sup> On 20 April 2017, Unilever acquired Sir Kensington's, a New York–based condiment maker.<sup about="#mwt251" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-71" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-71"}}'><a href="#cite_note-71" id="mwAhg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAhk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAho">[</span>71<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAhs">]</span></span></a></sup> On 15 May 2017, the company acquired the personal care and home care brands of Quala, a Latin American consumer goods company.<sup about="#mwt254" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-72" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-72"}}'><a href="#cite_note-72" id="mwAhw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAh0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAh4">[</span>72<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAh8">]</span></span></a></sup> In June, the company acquired Hourglass, a colour cosmetics brand.<sup about="#mwt257" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-73" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-73"}}'><a href="#cite_note-73" id="mwAiA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAiE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiI">[</span>73<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiM">]</span></span></a></sup> In July, the company then announced that it had acquired the organic herbal tea business, Pukka Herbs.<sup about="#mwt260" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-74" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-74"}}'><a href="#cite_note-74" id="mwAiQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAiU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiY">[</span>74<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAic">]</span></span></a></sup> In September 2017, Unilever acquired <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weis_(frozen_foods_company)" title="Weis (frozen foods company)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAig">Weis</a>, an Australian ice cream business.<sup about="#mwt263" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-75" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-75"}}'><a href="#cite_note-75" id="mwAik"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAio"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAis">[</span>75<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAiw">]</span></span></a></sup> Later that month Unilever acquired Remgro's interest in Unilever South Africa in exchange for the Unilever South Africa spreads business plus cash consideration.<sup about="#mwt266" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-76" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-76"}}'><a href="#cite_note-76" id="mwAi0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAi4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAi8">[</span>76<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjA">]</span></span></a></sup> Even later that month, Unilever agreed to acquire Carver Korea, a skincare business brand of AHC in Northeast Asia, for $2.7<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAjE"> </span>billion.<sup about="#mwt269" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-77" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-77"}}'><a href="#cite_note-77" id="mwAjI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAjM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjQ">[</span>77<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjU">]</span></span></a></sup> In October 2017, Unilever acquired Brazilian natural and organic food business Mãe Terra.<sup about="#mwt272" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-78" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-78"}}'><a href="#cite_note-78" id="mwAjY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAjc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjg">[</span>78<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAjk">]</span></span></a></sup> In November, Unilever announced an agreement to acquire the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tazo" title="Tazo" id="mwAjo">Tazo</a> speciality tea brand from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starbucks" title="Starbucks" id="mwAjs">Starbucks</a>.<sup about="#mwt275" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-79" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-79"}}'><a href="#cite_note-79" id="mwAjw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAj0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAj4">[</span>79<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAj8">]</span></span></a></sup> Later in November 2017, the company acquired Sundial Brands, a skincare company.<sup about="#mwt278" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-80" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-80"}}'><a href="#cite_note-80" id="mwAkA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkI">[</span>80<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkM">]</span></span></a></sup> In December 2017, Unilever acquired <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schmidt's_Naturals" title="Schmidt's Naturals" id="mwAkQ">Schmidt's Naturals</a>, a US natural deodorant and soap company.<sup about="#mwt281" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-81" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-81"}}'><a href="#cite_note-81" id="mwAkU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkc">[</span>81<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAkg">]</span></span></a></sup> In December 2017, Unilever sold its margarine and spreads division to investment firm <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kohlberg_Kravis_Roberts" title="Kohlberg Kravis Roberts" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAkk">KKR</a> for €6.8<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAko"> </span>billion.<sup about="#mwt284" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-82" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-82"}}'><a href="#cite_note-82" id="mwAks"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAkw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk0">[</span>82<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAk4">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt287" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-83" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-83"}}'><a href="#cite_note-83" id="mwAk8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlE">[</span>83<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlI">]</span></span></a></sup> The sale was completed in July 2018, and the new company was named <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Upfield_(company)" title="Upfield (company)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAlM">Upfield</a>.<sup about="#mwt290" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-84" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-84"}}'><a href="#cite_note-84" id="mwAlQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAlU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlY">[</span>84<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAlc">]</span></span></a></sup> Upfield's notable brands include <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flora_(margarine)" title="Flora (margarine)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAlg">Flora</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stork_(margarine)" title="Stork (margarine)" id="mwAlk">Stork</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I_Can't_Believe_It's_Not_Butter!" title="I Can't Believe It's Not Butter!" id="mwAlo">I Can't Believe It's Not Butter</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Band_(brand)" title="Blue Band (brand)" id="mwAls">Rama</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Country_Crock" title="Country Crock" id="mwAlw">Country Crock</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Becel" title="Becel" id="mwAl0">Becel</a>, and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Band_(brand)" title="Blue Band (brand)" id="mwAl4">Blue Band</a>.<sup about="#mwt293" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-85" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-85"}}'><a href="#cite_note-85" id="mwAl8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmE">[</span>85<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAmM">Unilever announced that to help tackle the global <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic" title="COVID-19 pandemic" id="mwAmQ">COVID-19 pandemic</a>, it would contribute over <span style="white-space: nowrap" about="#mwt294" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwAmU" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"€","href":"./Template:€"},"params":{},"i":0}}]}'>€</span>100<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAmY"> </span>million through donations of soap, hand sanitiser, bleach and food.<sup about="#mwt297" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-86" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-86"}}'><a href="#cite_note-86" id="mwAmc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmk">[</span>86<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAmo">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt300" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-87" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-87"}}'><a href="#cite_note-87" id="mwAms"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAmw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAm0">[</span>87<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAm4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwAm8" aria-labelledby="Since_2021"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Since_2021">Since 2021</h3></div>

<p id="mwAnA">In April 2021, Unilever established a new stand-alone beauty business, Elida Beauty, which will own and manage the following brands: Brut, Brylcreem, Timotei, Q-tips, Noxema, TIGI, VO5, Toni &amp; Guy, Matey, Moussel, Monsavon, Impulse, St Ives, Alberto Balsam, Badedas, Fissan, Pento, Pond's, Careess, Lever 2000, Williams, Elida, and Alberto.<sup about="#mwt303" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-88" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-88"}}'><a href="#cite_note-88" id="mwAnE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAnI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnM">[</span>88<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAnU">In August 2021, Florida governor <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ron_DeSantis" title="Ron DeSantis" id="mwAnY">Ron DeSantis</a> placed Unilever on a list of "Scrutinized Companies that Boycott Israel" because it had "no current plan to prevent Ben<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAnc"> </span>&amp;<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAng"> </span>Jerry's from terminating business activities in Israeli-controlled territories". The ice-cream brand has 90 days to stop engaging in "the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boycott,_Divestment_and_Sanctions" title="Boycott, Divestment and Sanctions" id="mwAnk">BDS movement</a>", or the state will no longer contract with the parent company Unilever or any of its subsidiaries.<sup about="#mwt306" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-89" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-89"}}'><a href="#cite_note-89" id="mwAno"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAns"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAnw">[</span>89<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAn0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAn4">In November 2021, Unilever agreed to sell most of its tea business under the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lipton_Teas_and_Infusions" title="Lipton Teas and Infusions" id="mwAn8">Ekaterra</a> division to investment firm <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CVC_Capital_Partners" title="CVC Capital Partners" id="mwAoA">CVC Capital Partners</a> for €4.5<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwAoE"> </span>billion. This deal excluded the Unilever tea business in India, Indonesia and Nepal, and the Lipton Ice Tea joint-venture with PepsiCo.<sup about="#mwt309" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-90" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-90"}}'><a href="#cite_note-90" id="mwAoI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoQ">[</span>90<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAoU">]</span></span></a></sup> The deal was completed in summer 2022.<sup about="#mwt312" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-91" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-91"}}'><a href="#cite_note-91" id="mwAoY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAoc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAog">[</span>91<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAok">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAoo">In December 2023, Unilever announced the company would sell Elida Beauty to Yellow Wood Partners, a private equity firm in the United States.<sup about="#mwt315" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-92" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-92"}}'><a href="#cite_note-92" id="mwAos"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAow"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo0">[</span>92<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAo4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAo8">In March 2024, Unilever announced plans to spin off its ice cream unit, which makes among others, brands such as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnum_(ice_cream)" title="Magnum (ice cream)" id="mwApA">Magnum</a> and Ben<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwApE"> </span>&amp;<span typeof="mw:Entity" id="mwApI"> </span>Jerry's, into a standalone business starting in March 2024 and planned to complete by the end of 2025.<sup about="#mwt318" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-93" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-93"}}'><a href="#cite_note-93" id="mwApM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApU">[</span>93<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApY">]</span></span></a></sup> The announcement was part of a cost-savings programme that would cut 7,500 jobs.<sup about="#mwt321" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-94" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-94"}}'><a href="#cite_note-94" id="mwApc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApk">[</span>94<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwApo">]</span></span></a></sup> In February 2025, Unilever announced that the ice cream unit would list on the Amsterdam stock market.<sup about="#mwt324" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-95" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-95"}}'><a href="#cite_note-95" id="mwAps"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwApw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp0">[</span>95<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAp4">]</span></span></a></sup> The ice cream unit, later known as <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Magnum_Ice_Cream_Company" title="The Magnum Ice Cream Company" id="mwAp8">The Magnum Ice Cream Company</a>, completed the demerger in November 2025.<sup about="#mwt327" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-96" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-96"}}'><a href="#cite_note-96" id="mwAqA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqI">[</span>96<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAqQ">In December 2024, the company announced the sale of food brand <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unox" title="Unox" id="mwAqU">Unox</a> and Zwan to Zwanenberg Food Group with the deal expected to be completed in 2026.<sup about="#mwt330" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-97" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-97"}}'><a href="#cite_note-97" id="mwAqY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAqc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqg">[</span>97<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAqk">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAqo">In June 2025, Unilever announced the acquisition of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dr._Squatch" title="Dr. Squatch" id="mwAqs">Dr. Squatch</a>, an American personal care brand, for $1.5 billion from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summit_Partners" title="Summit Partners" id="mwAqw">Summit Partners</a>.<sup about="#mwt333" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:4_98-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":4"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:4-98"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:4-98" id="mwAq0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAq4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAq8">[</span>98<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArA">]</span></span></a></sup> The deal remains subject to regulatory and shareholder approval.<sup about="#mwt334" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:4_98-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:4-98" id="mwArE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArM">[</span>98<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwArU">In March 2026, Unilever agreed to combine its food business with spice maker <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McCormick_&amp;_Company" title="McCormick &amp; Company" id="mwArY">McCormick &amp; Company</a>, creating a new sauces-to-spices company valued at more than $65 billion. Unilever shareholders were expected to own approximately 65% of the new company, and Unilever would also receive a one-time $15.7 billion cash payment. The deal excluded Unilever's food and tea businesses in India, Indonesia and Nepal, the Lipton Ice Tea joint-venture with PepsiCo, its Lifestyle Nutrition business and its Buavita business.<sup about="#mwt338" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-99" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-99"}}'><a href="#cite_note-99" id="mwArc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwArg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwArk">[</span>99<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAro">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwArs" aria-labelledby="Corporate_operations"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Corporate_operations">Corporate operations</h2></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwArw" aria-labelledby="Legal_structure"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Legal_structure">Legal structure</h3></div>
<figure class="mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAr0"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Unilever_Head_Office_Building_Rotterdam.jpg" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAr4"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Unilever_Head_Office_Building_Rotterdam.jpg" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Unilever_Head_Office_Building_Rotterdam.jpg/250px-Unilever_Head_Office_Building_Rotterdam.jpg" decoding="async" data-file-width="2304" data-file-height="3072" data-file-type="bitmap" height="200" width="150" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Unilever_Head_Office_Building_Rotterdam.jpg/330px-Unilever_Head_Office_Building_Rotterdam.jpg 2x" class="mw-file-element" id="mwAr8"/></a><figcaption id="mwAsA">Former head office building of Unilever N.V. which now became the HQ for the merged group's food and refreshments division, Rotterdam</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwAsE">Unilever's registered office is at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Sunlight" title="Port Sunlight" id="mwAsI">Port Sunlight</a> in Merseyside, United Kingdom, and its head office at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unilever_House" title="Unilever House" id="mwAsM">Unilever House</a> in London.<sup about="#mwt341" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-corpgov_100-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"corpgov"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-corpgov-100"}}'><a href="#cite_note-corpgov-100" id="mwAsQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsY">[</span>100<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAsc">]</span></span></a></sup> The company has been restructured several times, for example in 2018 and 2020 (see "history").<sup about="#mwt342" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-rest1_101-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"rest1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-rest1-101" id="mwAsg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAsk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAso">[</span>101<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAss">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt343" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-rest2_102-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"rest2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-rest2-102" id="mwAsw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAs0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAs4">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAs8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAtA">In 2018, Unilever announced its intention to simplify this structure by centralising the duality of legal entities and keeping just one headquarters in Rotterdam, abandoning the London head office. Business groups and staff would have been unaffected, as would the dual listing.<sup about="#mwt346" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-rest1_101-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"rest1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-rest1-101"}}'><a href="#cite_note-rest1-101" id="mwAtE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtM">[</span>101<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtQ">]</span></span></a></sup> On 5 October 2018 the group announced it would cancel the restructuring due to concern that the United Kingdom shareholders would lose value if the company fell out of the London FTSE100.<sup about="#mwt349" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-103" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-103"}}'><a href="#cite_note-103" id="mwAtU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAtY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtc">[</span>103<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt352" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-104" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-104"}}'><a href="#cite_note-104" id="mwAtk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAto"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAts">[</span>104<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAtw">]</span></span></a></sup> A shareholder vote was planned to decide for the listing of a new Unilever Dutch entity, which would have seen Unilever dropping out of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FTSE_100_Index" title="FTSE 100 Index" id="mwAt0">FTSE 100 Index</a>.<sup about="#mwt355" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-105" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-105"}}'><a href="#cite_note-105" id="mwAt4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAt8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuA">[</span>105<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuE">]</span></span></a></sup> When it appeared that the vote would fail, due to uncertainty over the Netherlands dividend tax, the scheme was cancelled on 5 October 2018.<sup about="#mwt358" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-106" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-106"}}'><a href="#cite_note-106" id="mwAuI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuQ">[</span>106<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAuY">In October 2018, the company acquired<sup about="#mwt361" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-107" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-107"}}'><a href="#cite_note-107" id="mwAuc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAug"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuk">[</span>107<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAuo">]</span></span></a></sup> a 75% stake in the Italian personal-care business Equilibra<sup about="#mwt364" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-108" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-108"}}'><a href="#cite_note-108" id="mwAus"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAuw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAu0">[</span>108<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAu4">]</span></span></a></sup> and acquired the high-end, eco-friendly laundry and household cleaning products company The Laundress for an undisclosed sum.<sup about="#mwt367" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-109" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-109"}}'><a href="#cite_note-109" id="mwAu8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvE">[</span>109<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvI">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2018, UK recruitment website, Indeed, named Unilever as the United Kingdom's ninth best private sector employer<sup about="#mwt370" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-110" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-110"}}'><a href="#cite_note-110" id="mwAvM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvU">[</span>110<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvY">]</span></span></a></sup> based on millions of employee ratings and reviews.<sup about="#mwt373" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-111" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-111"}}'><a href="#cite_note-111" id="mwAvc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAvg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvk">[</span>111<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAvo">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAvs">In 2020, Unilever announced after review of its corporate structure, the company was to merge Unilever N.V. into Unilever <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_limited_company" title="Public limited company" id="mwAvw">PLC</a> forming one holding company to be based in the United Kingdom.<sup about="#mwt376" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-auto_112-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"auto"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-auto-112"}}'><a href="#cite_note-auto-112" id="mwAv0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAv4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAv8">[</span>112<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwA">]</span></span></a></sup> However, a Dutch <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corporate_exit_tax" title="Corporate exit tax" id="mwAwE">exit tax</a> plan required the company to reconsider this unification.<sup about="#mwt379" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-rest2_102-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"rest2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-rest2-102"}}'><a href="#cite_note-rest2-102" id="mwAwI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAwM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwQ">[</span>102<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt382" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-113" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-113"}}'><a href="#cite_note-113" id="mwAwY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAwc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwg">[</span>113<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAwk">]</span></span></a></sup> In September 2020 Unilever's Dutch arm shareholders overwhelmingly voted for the N.V. to merge into the PLC.<sup about="#mwt385" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-114" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-114"}}'><a href="#cite_note-114" id="mwAwo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAws"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAww">[</span>114<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAw0">]</span></span></a></sup> In October 2020, Unilever announced that 99% of shareholders in its UK arm agreed with the merger, i.e., voted to base the group in London.<sup about="#mwt388" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-115" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-115"}}'><a href="#cite_note-115" id="mwAw4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAw8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxA">[</span>115<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxE">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt391" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-116" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-116"}}'><a href="#cite_note-116" id="mwAxI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxQ">[</span>116<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxU">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt394" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-117" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-117"}}'><a href="#cite_note-117" id="mwAxY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxg">[</span>117<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxk">]</span></span></a></sup> The completion of the unification was announced in November 2020. Since then there is one class of shares.<sup about="#mwt397" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-standard30nov_118-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"standard30nov"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-standard30nov-118"}}'><a href="#cite_note-standard30nov-118" id="mwAxo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAxs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAxw">[</span>118<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAx0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwAx4" aria-labelledby="Senior_management"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Senior_management">Senior management</h3></div>
<p id="mwAx8">In January 2019, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Jope" title="Alan Jope" id="mwAyA">Alan Jope</a> succeeded Paul Polman as the chief executive officer.<sup about="#mwt400" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-119" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-119"}}'><a href="#cite_note-119" id="mwAyE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyM">[</span>119<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyQ">]</span></span></a></sup> The chief financial officer, Graeme Pitkethly,<sup about="#mwt403" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-120" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-120"}}'><a href="#cite_note-120" id="mwAyU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyc">[</span>120<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyg">]</span></span></a></sup> is executive director. Jope will be proposed as joint executive director at Unilever's 2019 AGM.<sup about="#mwt406" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-121" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-121"}}'><a href="#cite_note-121" id="mwAyk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAyo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAys">[</span>121<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAyw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAy0">Previously, Paul Polman was CEO for ten years, succeeding Patrick Cescau in 2009.<sup about="#mwt409" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_122-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-122"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-122" id="mwAy4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAy8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzA">[</span>122<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAzI">In November 2019, Unilever announced that Nils Andersen would be replacing Chairman Marijn Dekkers, who stepped down after three years in the role.<sup about="#mwt412" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-123" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-123"}}'><a href="#cite_note-123" id="mwAzM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzU">[</span>123<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAzc">In January 2023, it announced <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hein_Schumacher" title="Hein Schumacher" id="mwAzg">Hein Schumacher</a> as its new CEO, effective July 2023.<sup about="#mwt415" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-124" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-124"}}'><a href="#cite_note-124" id="mwAzk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAzo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzs">[</span>124<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAzw">]</span></span></a></sup> In February 2025, Unilever announced Schumacher would step down on 31 May.<sup about="#mwt418" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-125" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-125"}}'><a href="#cite_note-125" id="mwAz0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAz4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAz8">[</span>125<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0A">]</span></span></a></sup> He was replaced by Fernando Fernandez.<sup about="#mwt421" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-126" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-126"}}'><a href="#cite_note-126" id="mwA0E"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA0I"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0M">[</span>126<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA0Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

